To optimize system performance, we must carefully balance these factors. For instance, in scenarios with high traffic density, quasi-TEM modes might be preferable to minimize latency and ensure timely data delivery. Conversely, in less densely populated areas, quasi-TE1 modes could be more energy-efficient, albeit with slightly higher latency.

