Adaptive nulling involves adjusting the phase and amplitude of the antenna elements to create nulls in the interference direction. This can be achieved using various techniques such as least-squares-based methods or adaptive array processing algorithms.

Interference cancellation involves estimating the interference signal and subtracting it from the received signal, thus effectively removing the interference. This can be achieved using techniques such as spatial filtering, successive interference cancellation, and blind source separation.

